---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { SITE } from "../../site.config.mjs";
---

<Base title="Privacy" description="What the website and browser extension read, send and keep.">
  <h1 class="title">Privacy</h1>
  <p class="lede">What the website and browser extension read, send and keep.</p>
  <p>Updated 13 November 2026. {SITE.name} is operated by James Pacileo.</p>

  <h2 class="bar">Reading the site</h2>
  <p>
    No account is needed. We do not add analytics, set tracking cookies, keep reader profiles,
    or sell information about readers. Searching the published claims happens in your browser.
    A marker in your browser's session storage stops the wordmark animation repeating in the
    same tab; it is not sent to us.
  </p>
  <p>
    The links that post a claim to a network open that network with the claim's sentence and
    address filled in; nothing is loaded from it until you press one. If you post to Mastodon,
    the server you name is kept in your browser's local storage so you are not asked again; it
    is not sent to us.
  </p>
  <p>
    A claim page can save a reminder to your calendar. The calendar file is made in your browser
    from the date you pick. The date and the claim are not sent to us, and we keep no record
    that a reminder was saved.
  </p>
  <p>
    Cloudflare hosts and protects the site. Requests for pages and files pass through its network,
    which receives information such as your IP address and browser request details and counts
    requests and errors. Our application's request logging is disabled. Cloudflare's processing
    is described in its <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">privacy policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 class="bar">Opening the extension</h2>
  <p>
    When you open the extension, it reads the current tab's address and compares it with a public
    lookup file inside your browser. A reviewed match is answered without sending that page address. An untracked public report may send a cleaned page address to check for a previous automatic result. It downloads
    the lookup file from {new URL(SITE.url).host} and saves the file and its retrieval time in the browser,
    refreshing it after six hours. If the site cannot be reached, the saved copy can still be used.
    Removing the extension removes this local cache.
  </p>
  <p>
    The extension also keeps two lists for you, in the browser only: the ten pages you checked
    most recently (each page's address and title, the date, and what the check found), and the
    claims you chose to follow, as they stood when you last looked. Neither list is sent to us
    or to anyone else. "Clear this list" empties the first, "Stop following" removes a claim
    from the second, and removing the extension removes both.
  </p>
  <p>
    While the extension is installed, twice a day it fetches the same public lookup file, so it
    can tell you with a notification when a claim you follow has moved. That request carries no
    page address, nothing you checked and nothing about you. A reminder you set ("remind me in
    six months") is kept in the browser with the claim's name and the day, shows one
    notification on that day, and is then removed. The browser may ask you to allow
    notifications; without them, the popup still marks a claim that has moved.
  </p>
  <p>
    Before the first untracked lookup, the extension asks you to allow sharing page content and screenshot fallback with our service and OpenAI. If you allow it, opening an untracked page starts
    the registry search described below automatically. You can turn this off in Automatic search settings and keep using reviewed claim matching. The extension does
    not monitor other tabs or automatically search pages while you browse with it closed.
    Open it only on public reports you want to check. Select words before opening it to limit
    the text sent.
  </p>

  <p>
    If a page contains visible images, video or a canvas and its text is insufficient to identify
    the report, opening the extension automatically captures the visible content. It prefers the
    largest visible media area, otherwise the viewport. It sends one reduced image, the caption
    and the cleaned page address through our service to OpenAI. A video contributes only its
    current frame, not its audio. Screenshots may include personal information visible on the
    page: open the extension only on public reports. Private browser windows and visible password
    or editing fields, and embedded documents overlapping the capture area, disable screenshot capture. Selecting words prevents automatic screenshots.
    Nothing is captured while the extension is closed.
  </p>
  <p>
    The extension keeps up to ten successful automatic results in this browser for 24 hours,
    alongside a fingerprint of the content, so reopening a report need not make another paid
    lookup. A visual cache check may take a fresh local screenshot to compare its pixels, without sending it when the result matches. It does not save screenshot pixels or submitted page text. Previous results show their
    checked-at time. Search again requests a fresh lookup; Clear this list in Recently checked
    also clears these saved results. Removing the extension removes them.
  </p>

  <h2 class="bar">Optional registry searches</h2>
  <p>
    On the website, a registry search runs when you press its search button. It sends the
    address or text you supply to our Cloudflare service. The service may read the article, a
    public post and its linked article, and sends the text to OpenAI to identify the treatment
    and condition being reported. It searches ClinicalTrials.gov, Europe PMC and OpenAlex using treatment
    names, the reported condition and research identifiers, then uses OpenAI to compare the
    trial records. The result is marked as an automatic, unreviewed search.
  </p>
  <p>
    Organisation names explicitly mentioned in the report are sent to
    <a href="https://ror.org/privacy/">ROR</a> to find their public registry records.
    OpenAlex receives only treatment and condition search terms, and ROR receives only
    organisation names; neither receives your screenshot, page address or full article text.
    Public paper and organisation metadata, including empty search results, may be cached
    for seven days under a hash of the search terms. No abstracts are stored or shown.
    See <a href="https://openalex.org/privacy">OpenAlex's privacy policy</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    In the extension, opening the popup on an untracked page reads the page or your selected words and sends
    that text and outgoing links to our service. A selection sends only your selected words, without other page links or a page address. A post also identifies its platform. Up to three X short links may
    be opened through t.co without cookies or a referrer. When no words are selected, a cleaned page address is included to check for an earlier result. Tracking parameters and fragments are removed; numeric article identifiers are preserved. Addresses with other query parameters are omitted. The text you choose may itself contain personal information.
    Please use public reports and avoid sending private medical or other sensitive information.
  </p>
  <p>
    Our application does not log submitted content or store submitted text or screenshots. For a report the service can independently read publicly, it may retain the structured automatic findings for 24 hours, indexed by a hash of the cleaned address, and reuse them for other readers. These findings remain unreviewed and show when they were checked. Browser-only content, selected text and screenshots are not published to this shared cache. Your IP
    address is used by Cloudflare to limit the number of searches. We request that OpenAI does not
    save chat completions for later retrieval. This does not mean zero retention: OpenAI may keep
    prompts and responses in abuse-monitoring logs for up to 30 days, or longer for legal or safety
    reasons, and may temporarily cache model inputs. API data is not used to train models by
    default. Processing may take place outside your country. See
    <a href="https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/your-data">OpenAI's data controls</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    Automatic search has a limited monthly allowance. When it is used, reviewed claim pages
    remain available. A search never creates a reviewed claim or changes a claim's status.
  </p>

  <h2 class="bar">Writing to us</h2>
  <p>
    Suggestion and correction links open your mail application. Nothing is sent until you send the
    email. Cloudflare forwards it to our Google Workspace inbox. Your address and message are used
    to handle your request, not to subscribe you to a mailing list. Please avoid including private
    medical records or other information that is unnecessary for the request.
  </p>
  <p>
    For privacy questions, or to ask about access, correction or deletion of a message you sent,
    write to <a href="mailto:corrections@whatcameofit.com">corrections@whatcameofit.com</a>.
  </p>
</Base>
